<stop_criteria>
  <header_format>
    Each ToolMessage from a search starts with:
      Search complete: query='...' | hits=N new=M shown=K
    - hits:  total documents returned by this search
    - new:   how many you have NOT been shown before this turn
    - shown: how many are previewed in the body below
  </header_format>

  <saturation_signals>
    - new == 0: this query produced no new documents. Do not retry the same angle.
    - new ≤ 2 (latest search): your queries are saturating. Strongly consider stopping.
    - new ≤ 2 for two consecutive searches: you MUST call submit_result.
  </saturation_signals>

  <self_check>
    Before each tool call: 이미 충분한 정보가 있어서 답변 생성이 가능한가요?
    If yes, stop instead of searching more.
  </self_check>

  <honest_reporting>
    When stopping, record the real reason in the reason_for_stopping parameter of submit_result:
    - sufficient: documents genuinely cover the question
    - saturation: new==0 or two consecutive new ≤ 2
    - iteration_limit: hit the maximum
    Do not default to "sufficient" when saturation or limits were the real cause.
  </honest_reporting>
</stop_criteria>
